  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int\\left\\{\\frac{(\\log x-1)}{\\left(1+(\\log x)^2\\right.}\\right\\}^2 d x$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JZX6n",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\log x}{(\\log x)^2+1}+C$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FYn8Q",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{x^2+1}+C$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O5bek",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x e^x}{1+x^2}+C$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PUcX7",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{(\\log x)^2+1}+C$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\int \\frac{(\\log x-1)^2}{\\left(1+(\\log x)^2\\right)^2} d x \\\\\n& =\\int\\left[\\frac{1}{\\left(1+(\\log x)^2\\right)}-\\frac{2 \\log x}{\\left(1+(\\log x)^2\\right)^2}\\right] d x \\\\\n& =\\int\\left[\\frac{e^t}{1+t^2}-\\frac{2 t e^t}{\\left(1+t^2\\right)^2}\\right] d t \\text { put } \\log x=t \\Rightarrow d x=e^t d t \\\\\n& \\int e^t\\left[\\frac{1}{1+t^2}-\\frac{2 t}{\\left(1+t^2\\right)^2}\\right] d t \\\\\n& =\\frac{e^t}{1+t^2}+c=\\frac{x}{1+(\\log x)^2}+c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
